{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"c08a277a-95ab-4c61-a12a-017ae9b475af","status":"SUCCESS","response":"**ANSWER.md**  \n*Path: `/tmp/h-Y0R1vi/ANSWER.md`*  \n\n---  \n\n## Why the launchd job produced no output  \n\n| # | Symptom | Root Cause |\n|---|---------|------------|\n| 1️⃣ | `nightly-review.err` contains multiple lines: `read-only variable: status` | The script defined `status=$?` after the `claude` command while `set -u` makes variables read‑only once they are assigned. Attempting to reassign `status` triggered a runtime error, aborting the script before any notification was sent. |\n| 2️⃣ | The same error repeats on every launch (the job never reaches the notification step). | Because the script exits on the read‑only error, the `if [ $status -ne 0 ]` block never runs correctly, so no Telegram message (success or failure) is emitted. |\n| 3️⃣ | `nightly-review.err` also shows `Not logged in · Please run /login` | The `claude` CLI requires a login token. When the job runs under launchd it does **not** inherit the interactive shell environment where the token is cached, so `claude` fails. This failure is now correctly captured by the exit‑status handling after the fix. |\n| 4️⃣ | `nightly-review.out` is empty | The script never reaches the final `notify.sh` call because it crashes earlier (read‑only variable). |\n\n## What was fixed  \n\n1. **Renamed the mutable exit‑status variable**  \n   ```zsh\n   exit_status=$?\n   if [ $exit_status -ne 0 ]; then\n   ```\n   This avoids the `read-only variable: status` error caused by `set -u`.  \n\n2. **Updated the failure‑notification message**  \n   The message now references the correct variable:  \n   ```zsh\n   \"$NOTIFY\" \"nightly review FAILED (exit $exit_status), see $OUT\"\n   ```\n   This ensures the user sees the actual exit code.  \n\n3. **Preserved the successful‑notification line** (unchanged) – it already uses the correct `$NOTIFY` call.  \n\n## Remaining considerations  \n\n- **`claude` authentication**: The job still fails with “Not logged in”. Ensure the API token or login session is available to launchd, e.g. by setting `CLAUDE_TOKEN` in the `\u003ckey\u003eEnvironmentVariables\u003c/key\u003e` section of the plist or by storing the token in a file that the script reads.  \n- **Permissions**: Verify that `nightly-review.zsh` and `notify.sh` are executable (`chmod +x`).  \n- **Log monitoring**: After applying the fixes, check `~/Library/Logs/nightly-review.out` and `.err` after the next scheduled run (02:30) to confirm that a Telegram message is sent.  \n\n---  \n\n**Summary**: The launchd job never reported because the script attempted to reassign a read‑only variable (`status`) under `set -u`, causing an immediate abort. Renaming the variable to `exit_status` and correcting the error‑handling message resolves the crash, allowing the script to reach the notification step. Further action is needed only to make the `claude` CLI authenticated for non‑interactive runs.  \n","duration_seconds":45.039904,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":12164,"output_tokens":3377,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":106176,"total_tokens":15541}}}
